17:       text: 'Agent-plugin version resolution never fails the marker: the scan of the plugin caches under the user profile (.codex/plugins/cache, .claude/plugins/cache, .grok/installed-plugins) skips any directory it cannot traverse (a link or other reparse point, an untrusted mount point, an inaccessible folder), and that covers each cache root itself and every folder between the user profile and it: a cache root that is a link, or that is reached through a link below the user profile (for example a linked .codex, .codex/plugins, .claude/plugins/cache or .grok), contributes no candidate, the same as a link inside the cache, while a user profile that is itself a link is still scanned; a version file (.version or a plugin manifest) that exists but cannot be read (an IO or access error) yields no version, so resolution goes on to the next file and the next candidate; and resolution falls back to the synced plugin version when nothing yields one. Any other error still propagates. Unit tests take every plugin-version input (the agent plugin-root environment variables, the workspace sibling plugin folder and the user profile caches) from test-owned data, never from the process environment, the machine or the real profile, and a full unit run under a hostile environment (every plugin-root variable and HOME pointed at scripted bad data) stays 0 failed (operator 2026-10-20: "Fix scans in PR 87 (Recommended)", "Fold R3-P3 in first" and "Structural fix, round 4 (Recommended)"; operator 2026-10-21: "Fix both, strengthen ACs", hostile validation round 5 finding R5-F1; IMPL-UNITGREEN-001, triage-report-b0e41c36f93c4c91b1bf2524eb579ef8).'
